NEARS-2932 — submit_product_review guest-id-collision demonstration

Live (port 8124): POST /api/v1/items/reviews/submit as customer id 6 with a
bogus order_id -> 403 {"code":"order_id","message":"Order data not found"}
(confirms the endpoint + error path are reachable/correct in this build).

The specific collision scenario (a GUEST order whose `user_id` column
equals the caller's own user id) requires a purpose-built fixture pairing
(Order.is_guest=1, Order.user_id == attacker's own User.id) that does not
exist in the live dev DB and would require a DB write to construct.
Substituted with the dedicated phpunit suite (isolated test DB):
  Nears2932SubmitReviewGuestIdCollisionTest (2/2 passed, 6 assertions):
   - an authenticated user CANNOT review a guest order whose user_id
     collides with their own id -> 403 order_data_not_found, AND no Review
     row is ever written.
   - anti-vacuity control: the same user's own genuine (non-guest) order
     still reviews successfully (200, Review row created).
